$1.4&nbsp;million and $1.7&nbsp;million, for the three months ended January&nbsp;31, 2026 and 2025, respectively. The difference between GAAP and <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">non-GAAP</FONT> gross margin was 1.5% and 2.2%, or $6.0&nbsp;million
and $6.3&nbsp;million, for the fiscal years ended January&nbsp;31, 2026 and 2025, respectively. The differences were due to the effect of stock-based compensation and amortization of acquisition-related costs. </P>
